{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1452631-m20-prime-sphere","id":1452631,"title":"M20 Prime Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-17T08:05:55-07:00","id":1452631,"title":"M20 Prime Sphere","content":"The Prime sphere has always confused me - I could never figure out exactly what Tass was or what do do with it (or how to use it). What exactly is a Soulflower or Soulgem - they're mentioned exactly once in the book with no explanation. What can one do with Prime? Some things are self-explanatory (as much as anything in Mage), but other things... not so much. To this end I started researching, both online (including on this forum) and throughout the books (note I only have access to the Revised core book, and all the M20 books) and I came up with the following. I believe it is basically the RAW for M20, with maybe just a bit of house rules and/or revisions thrown in.<br /> <br /> Comments are welcome. Do you think it represents the rules as written, or is it a departure from them? Is this more or less how one uses the Prime sphere, or am I way off?<br /> <br /> Also, do you think the proposed house rule makes sense, or is there something there that I am missing?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Raw quintessence</u></b> is that which is locked within a Pattern. The Raw quintessence in <b>Static</b> patterns (forces/matter) is fixed, but in <b>dynamic</b> patterns (life) this Raw quintessence is a continuous flow into and back out of the living being and is sometimes called the \u201cLife Force\u201d. In both cases, static and dynamic, this Raw quintessence is an integral part of the pattern and as a result it is difficult to access or manipulate.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Free Quintessence</u></b> is that which is NOT locked into a Pattern and it flows throughout the universe, occasionally accumulating in Nodes or in certain energetic events created by intense emotions or acts. Mages can access Free quintessence much more easily than Raw quintessence.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tass</u></b> is solidified quintessence which is often used as currency between mages. It occurs naturally at nodes or can be created with Prime 4. It can be utilized with Prime 1 to directly power an effect, or it can be broken down into Free quintessence with Prime 3.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Periapt/Matrix/Soulflower</u></b> is a kind of refillable Tass that can store quintessence. It is created with Prime 3 and either Matter 5 (Periapt/Matrix) or Life 5 (Soulflower) and is recharged like a living Avatar (storing it at a node, channeling quintessence into it w/ Prime 3+). Mechanically a periapt works as an additional quintessence/paradox wheel (on the mage character sheet) with five boxes per level of the Periapt (Wonder). When periapt-stored quintessence is used for a vulgar effect the paradox is added to the Periapt instead of the mage and if this causes a backlash it likewise affects the periapt, quite possibly destroying it. Paradox stored by a periapt dissipates naturally at a rate of 1/month (for matter-based periapts) or 1/week (for soulflowers). \u2018Matrix\u2019 is the name given to material periapts by the technocracy, and they do not have a special name for living periapts because they rarely (or never) use them. Quintessence stored in a periapt is considered Free, and so is relatively easy to access by any mage with Prime 1+.<br /> <br /> A material periapt will physically bond with the mage if kept in contact for a period of time (or consecrated with a Prime 1 effect), taking on that mage\u2019s Resonance \u2013 in this case the periapt\u2019s capacity to store quintessence is added to the mage\u2019s own, mechanically acting as a single expanded quintessence/paradox wheel. The advantage to this is that this additional capacity is considered Raw, just as though it were personal quintessence at or below the threshold of the mage\u2019s Avatar rating, and of course the periapt can no longer be physically taken from the mage or destroyed by a paradox backlash. On the inevitable downside, it creates the possibility that far more paradox can accumulate, which means that far more catastrophic backlashes become possible.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Proposed House Rule:</u></b> Quintessence can be expended to reduce the difficulty on an Arete roll, but the rules as written (RAW) do not allow the difficulty to be reduced by more than 3 and do not offer another use for it, so there is little point in having an Avatar rating higher than 3 or in using a Prime effect to allow oneself to expend additional quintessence beyond 3. There are many indications that a large quintessence expenditure should create massive effects, but nothing in the RAW seems to give quintessence this use. A proposed solution is that if the diff has already been reduced by 3 and if the Arete roll is successful, excess quintessence expended each gives a 1 success boost to the effect, but if the Arete roll is a failure or botch then this extra quintessence adds to paradox. For example, a mage casts a Forces 3 attack and is able to expend 10 quintessence. The first 3 reduce the Arete roll difficulty by 3, and if the roll is successful, then the attack is counted as though an additional 7 successes were gained on the Arete roll, creating a massive blast both physically and metaphysically (due to the large quintessence expenditure) that can be sensed by mages for miles around. If the roll was a failure or botch, however, the mage takes an additional 7 paradox \u2013 such power is not without risk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prime 1 \u2013 Perceive and Absorb Free Quintessence / Utilize Tass or Periapt / Consecrate / Anti-magick (ST optional)</b><br /> The Mage can perceive Free quintessence, allowing him to identify Nodes and the changes in flow caused by sphere magick, or sensing if another being is holding Free quintessence within their pattern. By meditating at a Node he can absorb personal quintessence into his pattern beyond what his Avatar would normally allow, but this excess personal quintessence is considered Free and therefore may be perceptible and vulnerable. The mage can utilize the quintessence stored in Tass and Periapts to directly power effects, though he cannot yet break Tass down into Free quintessence. A mage with basic knowledge of Prime can consecrate other patterns, giving them his own resonance so that even material objects will transform along with his body or translate into the spirit realms if he steps sideways. Consecrating stored quintessence \u2018cleanses\u2019 it, removing ill effects caused by absorbing energies that conflict with the mage\u2019s own resonance. Technomancers have an additional trick (storyteller optional) with Prime \u2013 similar to countermagick but instead of rolling Arete diff 7 they can roll their Prime rating diff 8, and instead of subtracting successes from the effect it increases the effect\u2019s difficulty by 1 per success.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime 2 \u2013 Fuel Pattern / Reinforce Static Pattern / Craft Trinket / Self-Sacrifice (Heart\u2019s Blood)</b><br /> Combined with a pattern sphere, the mage can now divert quintessence into new patterns, thus creating something from \u2018thin air\u2019. When not combined with a pattern sphere, this \u2018Body of Light\u2019 appears as a translucent hologram with no physical substance. A Prime 2 mage may also expend more quintessence than his Avatar would normally allow at an additional rate of 1 per success. With Forces or Matter 2, a static pattern can be reinforced to allow that pattern to inflict and/or withstand aggravated damage for the duration. Similarly, a static pattern can be enhanced with a single simple effect and infused with quintessence to make it permanent, creating a Trinket. By inverting the Fuel Pattern effect some mages trade the integrity of their own life force for additional power \u2013 for each unsoakable level of aggravated damage the mage accepts on himself, he can add one quintessence to directly fuel an effect and if this kills the mage that last level adds an additional 5 quintessence to the effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime 3 \u2013 Channel Free Quintessence / Perceive Raw Quintessence / Reinforce Dynamic Pattern / Energy Weapon / Craft Talisman or Periapt / Convert Tass / Lambs to the Slaughter</b><br /> The Mage can now channel Free quintessence as he wishes, infusing his own or another\u2019s pattern with it or refilling a periapt. The Prime 3 mage can also finally perceive Raw quintessence, seeing the actual life force and resonance of living beings and the full amount of quintessence that other mages have infused into their patterns. With Life 2 a dynamic (living) pattern can be reinforced to allow it to inflict or withstand aggravated damage for the duration. With Prime 3 alone and as a direct vulgar attack, he may \u201cRub the Bones\u201d, forcing the Raw quintessence within a pattern into flux and inflicting bashing damage against life/matter patterns or weakening a forces pattern and possibly causing it to dissipate. By expending a point of quintessence per attack he may create a destructive concentration of primal energy which manifests as a melee weapon or a ranged blast which inflicts aggravated damage. The Prime skilled mage can also create Talismans/Gadgets, which are like one-time-use Wonders, as well as Periapts, and break Tass down into Free quintessence that can be channeled as desired. By killing a living being as a sacrifice, the flow of Raw quintessence can briefly be diverted into an effect \u2013 this quintessence must be used immediately to directly fuel an effect but can offer a potent (and gruesomely Jhor-fueled) boost.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime 4 \u2013 Channel Static Raw Quintessence / Craft Tass and Wonders</b><br /> The mage can now channel the Raw quintessence within static patterns, dissipating it, infusing his own or another\u2019s pattern with it, or refilling a periapt, thereby destroying the forces/matter pattern in a vulgar display of power. The mage can also do the same to Tass, creating solid quintessence in whatever form he wishes. The mage can now also permanently infuse static patterns to create permanent Wonders.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime 5 \u2013 Channel Dynamic Raw Quintessence / Nullify Paradox / Create Node</b><br /> The mage can now channel the Raw quintessence within dynamic patterns, dissipating it, infusing his own or another\u2019s pattern with it, or refilling a periapt, thereby destroying the life pattern in a vulgar display of power. The mage can also Nullify Paradox (see Nullifying Paradox, p. 549) and manipulate the local flow of Free quintessence to such an extent that he can even create new nodes.<br /> <br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:26:10-07:00","id":1452635,"title":"","content":"One thing about the difficulty reduction you gain by spending Quintessence: it's a <i>net</i> limit of -3 difficulty, from <i>all</i> modifiers. So for example, if you have a modifier that's increasing your difficulty by one, you can spend four Quintessence to bring it down to a -3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:36:47-07:00","id":1452637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1452631-m20-prime-sphere?p=1452635#post1452635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about the difficulty reduction you gain by spending Quintessence: it's a <i>net</i> limit of -3 difficulty, from <i>all</i> modifiers. So for example, if you have a modifier that's increasing your difficulty by one, you can spend four Quintessence to bring it down to a -3.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, I always forget about that. Still, I feel like expending a large amount of quintessence should allow for impressively large effects, especially since quintessence is so hard to come by for any character that does not have access to a node and does not have Prime 4+.<br /> <br /> On that note, without a node how does a mage typically acquire quintessence? I've been playing Mage for awhile now and I've never taken the Node background, and because of this I basically have never ever spent quintessence which means some effects have just never been possible, and in general my character's power levels have lagged behind. Is Node just a 100% necessary background?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:47:07-07:00","id":1452648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1452631-m20-prime-sphere?p=1452637#post1452637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point, I always forget about that. Still, I feel like expending a large amount of quintessence should allow for impressively large effects, especially since quintessence is so hard to come by for any character that does not have access to a node and does not have Prime 4+.<br /> <br /> On that note, without a node how does a mage typically acquire quintessence? I've been playing Mage for awhile now and I've never taken the Node background, and because of this I basically have never ever spent quintessence which means some effects have just never been possible, and in general my character's power levels have lagged behind. Is Node just a 100% necessary background?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, access to a Node is the main method of acquiring Quintessence; high level Prime Sphere Effects can also help, including the ability to make your own Node at 5 dots. I don't know if a Node is 100% necessary, but it probably is if you do not have some kind of alternative (an amenable NPC with a Node to share, a reliable source of Tass that you can trade for, a cabal member with Prime skills). But one advantage is that a Node is a Background that can be shared and combined IIRC; if you have 3 or 4 other players, each of you can chip in just one Background point, and all of you have a Level 4 or 5 Node that you can share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-27T08:09:34-07:00","id":1453651,"title":"","content":"If you want to create a human being from nothing, you need to spend enough Quintessence to fuel the effect - we can see that a typical human-sized animal has 10 points of Quintessence in it in the rules, so investing at least 10 quintessence would be necessary. As a result, powerful command of Prime, with or without a powerful Avatar, is very important.<br /> <br /> That said, anything that requires 10+ points of Quintessence will likely be a feat demanding a lot of successes, and so the ability to infuse Quintessence quickly isn't necessarily that important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}